          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="4" column="0">
         <widget class="QLabel" name="hoverPrecisionLabel">
          <property name="text">
           <string>Precision</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="4" column="1">
         <widget class="QComboBox" name="hoverPrecisionComboBox">
          <property name="toolTip">
           <string>Whole rounds to the nearest unit. Fractional shows 2 decimals for bars and 1 for beats.</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="5" column="0">
         <widget class="QLabel" name="hoverLabelPositionLabel">
          <property name="text">
           <string>Label position</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="5" column="1">
         <widget class="QComboBox" name="hoverLabelPositionComboBox">
          <property name="toolTip">
           <string>Auto places the label right of the line, and left of it once the pointer passes three quarters of the overview.</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="6" column="0">
         <widget class="QLabel" name="hoverOverCueLabel">
          <property name="text">
           <string>Over a cue</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="6" column="1">
         <widget class="QComboBox" name="hoverOverCueComboBox">
          <property name="toolTip">
           <string>What to do when the pointer is over a cue, where Mixxx shows cue times. The beat distance is then measured to the cue. Join cue times: add it to the cue times. Hide hover readout: don't show it. Hide cue times: hide the cue times instead. Move hover readout: show it left of the cue line.</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="7" column="0" colspan="2">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="snapSeeksCheckBox">
          <property name="toolTip">
           <string>Clicking or dragging on the overview moves the play position by whole bars (or beats, see Unit) along the beat grid, keeping the play position's offset from the grid. The hover line snaps to the bar line (or beat) nearest the mouse. Applies to tracks with a beat grid.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>Snap seeks to beat distance</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
       </layout>
      </widget>
